    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Mild to moderate SLE not controlled on hydroxychloroquine, in patients who would otherwise be candidates for a course of corticosteroids: methotrexate 15-20 mg once a week, azathioprine 2 mg/kg/day or mycophenolate mofetil 1-1.5 g twice a day can be added, to keep corticosteroids at the lowest dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Belimumab (10 mg/kg IV every 2 weeks for 3 doses, then monthly, or 200 mg SC weekly) for uncontrolled disease or frequent flares; screen and monitor for depression and suicidality."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Severe disease (eg, lupus nephritis): corticosteroids plus cyclophosphamide or mycophenolate mofetil for induction; both need effective birth control. Cyclophosphamide beyond 6 months is discouraged (infertility, cancer); maintenance is mycophenolate or azathioprine."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Anifrolumab (anti-type I interferon receptor, 300 mg IV every 4 weeks) may be added for moderate to severe SLE, especially severe skin disease."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rituximab is an option for refractory thrombocytopenia and hemolytic anemia and, with a corticosteroid, an option (anecdotal evidence) for neuropsychiatric lupus."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
